# referenced by nothing in the build or the scripts.
/design

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- design handoff
#
# The handoff is NOT excluded wholesale, because part of it is load-bearing:
# `scripts/registry.ts` imports the registry .js files, so `npm run db:seed`,
# `verify:mapping` and `snapshot` all stop working without them. What is excluded
# is the ~4.4 MB of binaries, every one of which is a duplicate or already
# vendored:
#
#   *.webp     the same photos that /public/assets serves. The registries only
#              rewrite these paths as strings — nothing reads the handoff copies,
#              and verify:mapping resolves every asset against /public.
#   *.woff2    fonts, already in /public/assets/fonts.
#   .thumbnail design-tool artifacts.
#
# What stays is ~1.3 MB of text: the four registries (content provenance), the
# .dc.html prototypes (the stated pixel reference — the README cites them to
# settle two disagreements with the prose spec), the _ds bundle source that
# src/design-system was ported from, and the two spec documents.
arasya-handoff/**/*.webp
arasya-handoff/**/*.woff2
arasya-handoff/**/.thumbnail/
arasya-handoff/**/*.thumbnail
